Google Drive Setup

The project uses rclone to synchronize the Excel files stored in Google Drive with the Raspberry Pi.

The recommended setup is:

Google Drive
     │
     │ rclone
     ▼
Raspberry Pi
     │
     ▼
Local Excel files
     │
     ▼
rpi_stock_indicator

The Raspberry Pi runs the application using sudo, so the rclone configuration must be available to the user running the application.

1. Install rclone

On the Raspberry Pi:

sudo apt update
sudo apt install rclone

Verify:

rclone version
2. Configure Google Drive on a computer with a browser

If the Raspberry Pi is running without a GUI, it is easier to configure the Google Drive remote on a computer with a browser and then copy the rclone configuration to the Raspberry Pi.

In this example, the configuration is created on a Linux laptop.

Start rclone configuration:

rclone config

If an old/unused remote exists, it can be deleted:

Current remotes:

Name                 Type
====                 ====
dummy3005             drive

e) Edit existing remote
n) New remote
d) Delete remote
r) Rename remote
c) Copy remote
s) Set configuration password
q) Quit config

e/n/d/r/c/s/q> d

Select the remote to delete:

remote> 1

Then create a new remote:

n) New remote

n/s/q> n

Give the remote a name. For example:

name> hello_world3005
3. Select Google Drive

When rclone asks for the storage type, select:

13 / Google Drive
   "drive"

For example:

Storage> 13
4. Configure Google Drive access
Google Application Client ID

For the initial setup, leave this blank:

client_id>
OAuth Client Secret

Leave this blank:

client_secret>
Drive scope

Select full access because this project needs to read and update the Excel files:

1 / Full access all files, excluding Application Data Folder.
   "drive"

scope> 1
Root folder ID

If the project needs to use a specific Google Drive folder, enter its folder ID:

root_folder_id> <GOOGLE_DRIVE_FOLDER_ID>

For example:

root_folder_id> 1MPS_dQotGwQ8RwFtn8F4pLY3cZJ8WTp5

If the project should use the normal Google Drive root, leave this blank.

Note: The folder ID can be obtained from the Google Drive URL. For example, in:

https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1MPS_dQotGwQ8RwFtn8F4pLY3cZJ8WTp5

the folder ID is:

1MPS_dQotGwQ8RwFtn8F4pLY3cZJ8WTp5

Service account

Leave this blank unless a service account is specifically being used:

service_account_file>
5. Authenticate Google Drive

When rclone asks:

Edit advanced config?
y) Yes
n) No (default)

y/n>

Normally select:

n

For a computer with a browser, use automatic authentication:

Use auto config?
y) Yes (default)
n) No

Select:

y

A browser window will open.

Log in using the Google account containing the Excel files and authorize rclone.

After successful authentication, rclone will display the remote configuration.

Confirm it:

y) Yes this is OK (default)
e) Edit this remote
d) Delete this remote

y/e/d> y

Finally:

q

to quit.

6. Verify the Google Drive remote

List configured remotes:

rclone listremotes

Expected:

hello_world3005:

List directories:

rclone lsd hello_world3005:

For example:

          -1 2026-08-12 21:47:00        -1 folder1

List files:

rclone lsf hello_world3005:

Example:

folder1/
hello.docx

The : after the remote name is important:

rclone lsf hello_world3005:

not:

rclone lsf hello_world3005
7. Copy the rclone configuration to the Raspberry Pi

The rclone configuration is stored on the computer at:

~/.config/rclone/rclone.conf

This file contains authentication information. Do not commit it to GitHub or share it publicly.

On the computer, copy it to the Raspberry Pi:

scp ~/.config/rclone/rclone.conf dash@192.168.31.81:~/.config/rclone/

If the directory doesn't exist on the Pi:

ssh dash@192.168.31.81

Then:

mkdir -p ~/.config/rclone

Exit the SSH session and repeat the scp command.

8. Verify rclone on the Raspberry Pi

On the Raspberry Pi:

rclone listremotes

Expected:

hello_world3005:

Test:

rclone lsd hello_world3005:

and:

rclone lsf hello_world3005:

The Raspberry Pi should see the same Google Drive contents as the computer.
